/-!
# Seven-letter block selection from the original source action

The natural six-space and exceptional four-space branches of C.1.24(a)
construct their local seeds and yield either a nonzero characteristic
subgroup of the original Baumann group normal in G, or a block on the
original component. The normal-layer comparison then recognizes its
ordinary or exceptional A₇ type from the original full moved module.

The upstream B.5 source classification supplies the action alternatives;
neither source branch assumes a block or shortness. The possible central
triple cover is retained throughout the selection and generation arguments.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith C.1.24(a), printed pp.130–131. The application is
the A₇ branch preceding 13.6.22, printed p.932.
-/
